1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,784
听：A Headline Worth Checking.

2
00:00:02,784 --> 00:00:05,568
跟读：A Headline Worth Checking.

3
00:00:05,568 --> 00:00:28,368
听：Sara saw a headline claiming that a new study had proved online learning was always better. The article was popular, and several friends shared it immediately. Before forwarding it, Sara looked for the original source. She wanted to know what the researchers had actually measured.

4
00:00:28,368 --> 00:00:51,168
跟读：Sara saw a headline claiming that a new study had proved online learning was always better. The article was popular, and several friends shared it immediately. Before forwarding it, Sara looked for the original source. She wanted to know what the researchers had actually measured.

5
00:00:51,168 --> 00:01:16,056
听：The study involved a small sample of adults who had volunteered for an evening course. Their results could not automatically represent every learner. The article also omitted a limitation: the two groups had different amounts of support. Sara began to question whether the headline matched the evidence.

6
00:01:16,056 --> 00:01:40,944
跟读：The study involved a small sample of adults who had volunteered for an evening course. Their results could not automatically represent every learner. The article also omitted a limitation: the two groups had different amounts of support. Sara began to question whether the headline matched the evidence.

7
00:01:40,944 --> 00:02:10,032
听：Although the report contained useful findings, its conclusion was narrower than the headline suggested. Despite the confident wording, the researchers had not compared every form of education. Sara checked the publication date and looked for independent coverage. Repetition across several websites did not necessarily mean independent confirmation.

8
00:02:10,032 --> 00:02:39,120
跟读：Although the report contained useful findings, its conclusion was narrower than the headline suggested. Despite the confident wording, the researchers had not compared every form of education. Sara checked the publication date and looked for independent coverage. Repetition across several websites did not necessarily mean independent confirmation.

9
00:02:39,120 --> 00:03:06,624
听：She sent her friends a short correction and a link to the study. Rather than calling the whole report worthless, she explained the uncertainty. She also mentioned possible bias in the recruitment process. The conversation became more thoughtful when everyone distinguished a persuasive claim from a conclusion supported by adequate evidence.

10
00:03:06,624 --> 00:03:34,128
跟读：She sent her friends a short correction and a link to the study. Rather than calling the whole report worthless, she explained the uncertainty. She also mentioned possible bias in the recruitment process. The conversation became more thoughtful when everyone distinguished a persuasive claim from a conclusion supported by adequate evidence.
